  {
    "storyId": "MOCK-HW-1",
    "verdict": "needs_review",
    "reviewNotes": "Openspec correctly identified the defect nature, fix site (getGreeting in src/hello.ts), and produced a logical impl/test split. However, both child stories (MOCK-HW-1-impl, MOCK-HW-1-test) have empty acceptanceCriteria arrays — a gap that speckit would likely have caught had it been assigned. Even for trivial stories, children should carry concrete, testable AC (e.g., 'getGreeting() returns \"hello dolly\"' for impl; 'test assertion matches \"hello dolly\"' for test). The coordinator's decision to skip speckit is understandable for a mock story, but the result is incomplete specs on the children that will actually be implemented.",
